From: d012 setup <setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] The Android APK can carry a texture pack in its assets

build_apk.sh takes TEXTURE_DIR (optional): the folder goes into the APK assets under textures/, with textures/manifest.txt listing every file and its size, since an app cannot list its assets. Nothing changes without it.
---

diff --git a/packaging/android/build_apk.sh b/packaging/android/build_apk.sh
index 5d1e625..484144d 100755
--- a/packaging/android/build_apk.sh
+++ b/packaging/android/build_apk.sh
@@ -21,6 +21,8 @@
 # assets, and the app unpacks the font on its first start. Without it the
 # game's text is blank unless the device has a font stb_truetype reads.
 #
+# TEXTURE_DIR (optional): see below; it makes the APK as large as the pack.
+#
 # ANDROID_HOME must name the SDK (build-tools and a platform are needed).
 # DEBUGGABLE=1 marks the app debuggable, so `adb shell run-as` reaches its
 # files (its log, its data) on a test device; leave it out for players.
@@ -83,6 +85,16 @@ if [[ -n "${FONT_DIR:-}" ]]; then
     cp "$FONT_DIR/NotoSansCJKjp-Regular.otf" "$work/assets/fonts/"
     cp "$FONT_DIR/NotoSansCJK-LICENSE.txt" "$work/assets/licenses/NotoSansCJK-OFL.txt"
 fi
+# TEXTURE_DIR may name the textures folder of a game (the one that holds a folder per disc id, each with textures.ini): it goes into the
+# APK's assets under textures/, with textures/manifest.txt listing every file and its size (an app cannot list its assets), and the app
+# unpacks it on its first start, so the HD pack is there without the player importing anything.
+if [[ -n "${TEXTURE_DIR:-}" ]]; then
+    mkdir -p "$work/assets/textures"
+    cp -r "$TEXTURE_DIR"/. "$work/assets/textures/"
+    (cd "$work/assets/textures" && find . -type f ! -name manifest.txt | sed 's|^\./||' | sort | while IFS= read -r f; do
+        printf '%s\t%s\n' "$f" "$(wc -c < "$f" | tr -d ' ')"
+    done > manifest.txt)
+fi
 assets=(-A "$work/assets")
 "$build_tools/aapt2" compile --dir "$here/res" -o "$work/res.zip"
 "$build_tools/aapt2" compile --dir "$game_res" -o "$work/game-res.zip"
